# Site overrides for cross-building vxWorks/ppc604 from a Linux host.
#
# Install into $EPICS/base/config/. This is the override point EPICS 3.13.4
# already documents: CONFIG_SITE.Vx.Linux ends with
#   -include $(EPICS_BASE)/config/CONFIG_SITE.$(BUILD_TYPE).$(HOST_ARCH).$(T_A)
# and ships commented-out ORNL SNS examples of exactly this, for Tornado 2.0
# on Linux with a self-built powerpc-wrs-vxworks gcc.
#
# WHY IT IS NEEDED. CONFIG_HOST_ARCH.Linux line 8 sets
#     WIND_HOST_TYPE = Linux
# and CONFIG.Vx line 20 derives
#     VX_GNU_YES = $(VX_DIR)/host/$(WIND_HOST_TYPE)
# so the build looks for $WIND_BASE/host/Linux/bin/ccppc. ANL's Linux rebuild
# of the Wind River tools unpacks into host/x86-linux, not host/Linux, so the
# compile fails with "No such file or directory ... Error 127" -- and setting
# WIND_HOST_TYPE in the environment does not help, because an assignment in a
# makefile beats the environment.
#
# Overriding VX_GNU_YES rather than WIND_HOST_TYPE keeps the change scoped to
# where the toolchain is looked up; WIND_HOST_TYPE is also used to name host
# tool directories, which we do not want to move.
VX_GNU_YES = $(VX_DIR)/host/x86-linux
